1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:08,900
Before I talk to him, are we agreeing on a sentence? Anything from New York?

2
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:20,800
No cap on the sentence. No deal with New York. He pleads to what's left; sentencing is up to the judge.

3
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,710
Put that in writing. All of it.

4
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:38,510
Send it to my work address, please. I need him to read the same thing I have.

5
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:59,000
I can't make Sunday lunch. If the boiler guy comes, get the invoice before you pay. Call me back.

6
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:19,430
You plead guilty to the federal charges. Then we ask New York to drop its case.

7
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,940
Ask? You can't make them?

8
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:34,800
No. They'll argue an exception applies. The judge could agree with them.

9
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:38,080
Then why do this first?

10
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:45,210
Because that's the sequence for this motion. Not because we know it'll work.

11
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,660
And if I don't plead?

12
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:57,360
We prepare for trial. I'm not asking you to decide in this room.

13
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:08,230
So they could use my answers against me.

14
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:18,030
Yes. And even if New York drops the case, the federal judge could still give you life.

15
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:25,710
I thought the paper said something else.

16
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,640
Show me.

17
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:31,670
No. I read 'request' as 'agreement.'

18
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:43,230
Leave this with me. I'm not signing yet.

19
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:46,210
Fine. Tomorrow, same time.

20
00:02:55,800 --> 00:03:02,330
I read it twice. I want to plead guilty. Both federal counts.

21
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:06,360
Okay. What haven't we been promised?

22
00:03:07,010 --> 00:03:11,970
My sentence. New York dropping its case. Getting out.

23
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:27,850
Do you want me to ask for another meeting before I notify them?

24
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:37,130
No. Tell them I want to plead. I know the judge still has to ask me.

25
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:57,800
It's my decision. When you talk to the press, don't call it a win.

26
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:02,800
You can read it before it goes out.

27
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:13,300
Can I call my mom before the hearing? I need to tell her myself.

28
00:04:13,950 --> 00:04:16,000
I'll request the call.
